('Cleaning and storage for compact devices','''A small toy still needs careful cleaning. Follow the manufacturer’s instructions, avoid getting moisture into ports unless the product is clearly designed for it, and dry the device before storage. Store charging cables separately but nearby, so you do not have to guess later. If the surface becomes sticky, cracked, rough, or discolored, stop using it and contact support.
For travel, pack the toy clean, dry, and powered off. TSA guidance on electronics is useful for ordinary screening expectations, but travelers should also check destination laws. A discreet pouch helps protect privacy and keeps the device from collecting lint.'''),
